{"about":{"source":"econ/21-verification-costs/data/{case_results.csv,break_even.json,cost_scenarios.csv,summary.csv,verification_summary.json}; README.md","invoice_rows.columns":"row order of invoice_rows: id=test invoice id (72 test invoices test-001..); method=route code name; automatic=route paid an answer automatically (false = sent to a person/unresolved); correct=automatic and exact (decision AND amount to the cent match the rule program); answer_status=PAY|HOLD|REVIEW as returned by the route (REVIEW=sent to person); gold_status=exact decision; gpt_invocations=GPT calls billed for this invoice in this route (0/1); known_model_cost=USD of Qwen (OpenRouter metered) + Claude (list price) for this invoice, excludes assumed GPT price and human review; payment_deviation_usd=absolute dollars over+under paid vs the exact amount (0 if not automatic)","methods":"5 routes: Qwen direct, GPT direct, Qwen repeat + GPT, Claude screen + review, Claude screen + GPT","cost_lines":"per method, mean per invoice over the 72 test invoices: known_model_cost_mean (USD), gpt_invocations_mean, review_fraction (invoices sent to a person), mean_overpayment_exposure_usd, mean_underpayment_exposure_usd. Mean cost per invoice = known + G*gpt + H*review + a*over + b*under, where G=GPT price per call, H=human review cost (USD 1), a=overpayment loss fraction, b=underpayment loss fraction (README running example G=0.05,a=0.01,b=0.001). Derived here; verified to reproduce all 60 rows of cost_scenarios.csv (max abs error ~1e-12).","cost_lines.at_zero_loss":"intercept_zero_loss = known + H*review (+loss terms 0); slope_in_G = gpt_invocations_mean. cost = intercept + slope*G when a=b=0.","break_even":"zero_loss_break_even_gpt_price in USD per GPT call, from break_even.json; recomputed = (known_route - known_GPTdirect)/(gpt_GPTdirect - gpt_route)","summary":"summary.csv: n=72, automatic_correct, automatic_wrong, review counts, coverage, correct_fraction with 95% Wilson interval","illustrative_exam